course: dictionary
lesson: 14780
title: Proximity: how near something is
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Proximity is a noun. It means how near something is to something else. When you say things are in close proximity, you mean they are very near each other.
explain: «The house is in close proximity to the school.» This means the house is very near the school. You could say «The house is close to the school», and the meaning is almost the same, but proximity sounds more formal.
explain: Proximity can also be about time or relationships. «The test is in close proximity to the holidays» means the test is very near the holidays in time. Use the words around it to work out which kind of nearness is meant.
fact: Proximity is a noun, and it is uncountable, so do not add an s to it.
fact: «Proximity» means being near in space, time or relationship.
fact: «In close proximity to» means very near to.
fact: «Keep in close proximity to an adult» means stay near an adult, for safety.
fact: Proximity is a formal word, so you will often see it in science, geography and exam writing.
exercise: «The shop is in close proximity to the park.» What does proximity mean here? | Being inside | Being far away | Being quiet | *Being near
exercise: Mum says, «Keep in close proximity to an adult when we cross the road.» What should you do? | Wait far away from her | *Stay near an adult | Cross the road alone | Run ahead
exercise: «The station is in the proximity of the river.» What does «in the proximity of» mean? | *Near the river | On top of a bridge | Far from the river | Inside the river
test: «Plants in close proximity compete for light.» What does «close proximity» mean? | Far apart | Growing very fast | *Very near each other | Under water
test: In maths, what does proximity tell us about two points? | How heavy they are | The time it takes to reach them | How many sides they have | *How near the two points are
exam: What is the best meaning of proximity in «the proximity of the school»? | Noise | Dampness | *Nearness | Depth
